---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import MotionStage from '@/components/motion/MotionStage.astro';
import MotionUsage from '@/components/motion/MotionUsage.astro';
import MotionOptions from '@/components/motion/MotionOptions.astro';
import MotionTokens from '@/components/motion/MotionTokens.astro';
import Gestures from '@/components/motion/scenes/Gestures.astro';
import GesturesControls from '@/components/motion/scenes/GesturesControls.astro';
import { MotionGestureReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-gesture.tsx';
import { MotionGestureAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-gesture.ts';
import MotionGestureSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-gesture.svelte';
---
<MotionPage
  slug="gestures"
  title="Motion: drag, swipe, reorder"
  description="Drag, swipe and reorder with the pointer, each with the keyboard alternative it must have. In HTML, React, Angular and Svelte."
>
  <MotionStage scene="gestures" label="Live example: Drag, swipe, reorder" height={[416, 536]}>
    <Fragment slot="controls"><GesturesControls size="page" /></Fragment>
    <Gestures size="page" />
    <Fragment slot="readout"><span data-gestures-readout>no event yet</span></Fragment>
  </MotionStage>

  <h2>How to use it</h2>
  <p>
    A gesture moves an element with the pointer, and gives it a keyboard alternative, so the page works without one.
    Define it once, from <code>@udixio/motion/gesture</code>, and name it on the element with
    <code>data-motion-gesture</code>. An element carries one gesture at a time.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`import { defineGesture } from '@udixio/motion/gesture';

defineGesture('complete', { kind: 'swipe', alternative: 'action' });`}</code></pre>
  <pre><code>{`<div data-motion-gesture="complete">Send the invoice</div>

import { connectMotion } from '@udixio/motion';
connectMotion(); // binds data-motion-gesture like data-motion`}</code></pre>

  <h2>The three kinds</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>drag</code> follows the pointer on <code>axis</code> <code>x</code>, <code>y</code> or <code>both</code> (the
      default). It stays within its parent, or moves freely with <code>bounds: 'none'</code>. Released, it is thrown on by
      0.2 s of its velocity, within its bounds, and glides there with the release spring. Its alternative is
      <code>arrows</code>: the arrow keys move it 16 px, or 64 px with Shift.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>swipe</code> follows the pointer on <code>axis</code> <code>x</code> (the default) or <code>y</code>. Released
      past 40 % of its size, or at more than 800 px/s in its direction, it flies out and fades; released sooner, it springs
      back. Its alternative is <code>action</code>: Delete or Backspace swipes the focused element towards the end.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>reorder</code> moves the element among its siblings that carry the same gesture, on <code>axis</code>
      <code>y</code> (the default) or <code>x</code>, each time its centre crosses a neighbour's. Its alternative is
      <code>grab</code>: Space or Enter grabs the focused element, the arrow keys of its axis move it, Space or Enter drops
      it, and Escape puts it back where it was.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Events</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>motion-dragend</code>, with <code>detail: &#123; x, y &#125;</code>, when a released drag has come to rest. It cannot be prevented.</li>
    <li>
      <code>motion-swipe</code>, with <code>detail: &#123; direction &#125;</code> (<code>'start'</code> or
      <code>'end'</code>), when a swipe is released far or fast enough, or Delete is pressed. It is cancelable:
      <code>preventDefault()</code> keeps the element where it is, and it springs back. Without it, the element flies out and
      is <code>aria-hidden="true"</code> once out of sight; removing it is the page's job.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>motion-reorder</code>, with <code>detail: &#123; from, to &#125;</code>, before each step of a reorder, by pointer
      or by keyboard. It is cancelable: <code>preventDefault()</code> refuses the step.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>A reorder announces each keyboard step in a visually hidden live region, for example <code>Moved. Position 3 of 3.</code></p>

  <h2>Use it in the frameworks</h2>
  <p>
    React <code>&lt;Motion name="reflow" gesture="reorder" onMotionReorder&gt;</code>, with the move prevented and the state moved;
    Angular <code>udxMotionGesture="reorder"</code> with the <code>(udxReorder)</code> and <code>(udxSwipe)</code> outputs;
    Svelte <code>&#123;&#64;attach motionGesture('reorder', () =&gt; (&#123; onReorder &#125;))&#125;</code>. The examples
    reorder three tasks and swipe a card away; Restore brings the card back.
  </p>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-gesture">
    <MotionGestureReact slot="react" client:visible />
    <MotionGestureAngular slot="angular" client:visible />
    <MotionGestureSvelte slot="svelte" client:visible />
  </MotionUsage>

  <h2>Options</h2>
  <MotionOptions
    rows={[
      { name: 'kind', values: 'drag · swipe · reorder', description: 'What the pointer does with the element. Required.' },
      { name: 'axis', values: 'x · y (swipe, reorder); x · y · both (drag)', default: 'x, y, both', description: 'The axis the element moves along: x for a swipe, y for a reorder, both for a drag.' },
      { name: 'bounds', values: 'parent · none', default: 'parent', description: 'A drag stays within its parent, or moves freely. Drag only.' },
      { name: 'release', values: 'spring.* token', default: 'spring.default.spatial', description: 'The spring of the release, when the element comes to rest.' },
      { name: 'alternative', values: 'arrows · action · grab', description: 'The keyboard alternative of its kind. Required, and it must be the one of the kind.' },
    ]}
  />

  <h2>Timing and tokens</h2>
  <p>A release moves on a spring: the default for each gesture, or the one its definition names. The sticker of the hero uses the slow one.</p>
  <MotionTokens tokens={['spring.default.spatial', 'spring.slow.spatial']} />

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <p>
    Under reduced motion, or with <code>--udx-motion: none</code> on the element, a gesture's release is written at once,
    with no glide. The keyboard alternatives are unchanged.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A gesture writes the <code>translate</code> of its element, and its <code>opacity</code> while a swipe flies out. An author's <code>translate</code> on that element is overwritten while it is bound.</li>
    <li><code>touch-action</code> is set when the gesture is bound, so a touch screen does not scroll the page instead of moving the element. It is given back on <code>destroy()</code>.</li>
    <li>A drag is bounded by the content box of its parent, measured when the pointer grabs the element and at each nudge of a key.</li>
    <li>A reorder moves an element among the siblings that carry the same gesture, under the same parent.</li>
    <li>A swipe that is not prevented stays in the DOM, with <code>aria-hidden="true"</code>.</li>
    <li>A gesture's spec is validated in development only; its name is checked always.</li>
  </ul>
</MotionPage>
